# netops-demo · Architecture & Design Rationale

> An **operational-intelligence layer** on top of a **network digital twin**:
> **automatic incident detection → root-cause analysis (validated by counterfactual replay) → predictive capacity / SLA management**,
> where every conclusion is verifiable, reproducible, and statistically defensible.
> Setting: a telecom backbone operator (Orange Wholesale internship prototype). Code and comments are English; operator-facing traces are French.

---

## 0. Executive summary (the one-paragraph pitch)

From production device configuration, a pipeline stands up a faithful **emulated copy of a network zone** so changes can be tested safely before touching production. On top of that twin, this project delivers two capabilities and a rigorous way to trust them:

1. **Heartbeat detection** — a periodic patrol that turns raw telemetry, control-plane events, and config drift into structured `Incident`s.
2. **Root-cause analysis** — an agentic loop that reasons across *heterogeneous evidence* (config text, telemetry time-series, topology graph, BGP/IS-IS state), ranks candidate causes while **distinguishing cause from effect**, and **confirms the top hypothesis by re-injecting it into a sandbox copy of the twin** before concluding.
3. A third, forward-looking layer composes a **time-series forecaster** with a **steady-state performance model (RouteNet-Fermi)** so a forecast of *utilisation* becomes a forecast of *SLA breach probability*, emitted as a preventive `Incident(source="prediction")` into the same pipeline.

The central engineering property: **every mock names the real backend it stands in for. Swapping the simulation for the real system (EVE-NG + junos-mcp-server + gNMI + Batfish) is a matter of implementing an interface, not rewriting logic.** Everything runs **offline, deterministically, with zero required dependencies** beyond `networkx` + `numpy`.

