## 1. The problems being solved

| Layer | Problem | Deliverable |
|---|---|---|
| **Detection** | Can we find an incident **automatically and fast**? | `heartbeat/` |
| **Root cause** | Can we **separate cause from effect** and name the true source (not the *congested link*, which is a symptom)? | `rca/` agent |
| **Validation** | How do we **prove** a root-cause hypothesis without touching the real network? | `counterfactual.py` |
| **Prediction** | Can we warn **before** the fault happens (capacity / SLA)? | `prediction/` + `perf/` |
| **Evaluation** | Is the claim *"model A beats model B"* **defensible** rather than eyeballed? | `prediction/benchmark/` |

**Evaluation philosophy that drives the whole design:** judge the agent on whether it **gets the job done** under controlled failures — does it detect, does it name the true root cause, does it identify the right affected clients — **not** on how fluently it explains itself.

