| Cross-topology generalisation | currently only **same-topology cross-routing**; cross-topology needs extra EVE-NG zones |
| Preventive action | prediction emits an **intent** only; the twin-validated, gated preventive change is a commented seam |
| Nautilus `LiveDataClient` | gNMI live wrapper left as deployment wiring; the feed, data type and actor are shipped and tested |

> **Honesty statement.** The demo's analytic baseline is already strong (it is essentially the sim's own physics). RouteNet-Fermi's skill is a *non-circular, measurable* result against finite-buffer M/M/1/K labels. Its **architectural value** (SLA-prediction chain + millisecond counterfactual oracle + data-driven seam) holds in the demo; its **real-network value** (learning from measurements when queueing has no closed form, and cross-topology transfer — the paper's contribution) is marked as a clean seam and **not faked**.

